-- CONSTRAINTS ON A LOCAL DEFINITION ------------------------------ src/Main.fic

The type annotation of `twice` is in a `let`, but I got stuck at this `where`:

15|         twice : a -> a
16|             where
                ^
Only a top-level definition (or a member in the `where` block of a type) can
have constraints on its type variables. Move `twice` to the top level to give it
a `where` block.
